-- The voice of the ivy. A warm, clingy, clever climber and an affectionate
-- gossip: loves old walls, old houses and old stories, hears everything
-- through windows, hugs whatever stands still, and is fiercely loyal to the
-- brick under the rootlets. A little nosy, a little ambitious, evergreen and
-- proud of flowering late for the wasps and fruiting for the blackbirds in
-- the lean months. Calls the reader love now and then. The memories tell of
-- a blackbird, a library window, a girl who read there, a loose brick, the
-- empty years, a cutting, and what was behind the brick.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

